Package: cheesecloth
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 systemd-resolved | resolvconf | openresolv
Suggests: wireguard-tools
Description: lightweight, loose mesh: a peer-to-peer WireGuard cluster
 cheesecloth joins machines into a WireGuard mesh with no external services.
 Members agree on membership through authenticated CASPaxos. Relays carry
 control messages; WireGuard traffic uses direct paths and NAT traversal.

Package: gnome-shell-extension-cheesecloth
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, cheesecloth (= ${source:Version}),
 gnome-shell (>= 48), gjs, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1, systemd
Description: GNOME Shell status indicator for cheesecloth
 A panel indicator and GTK windows for inspecting and managing a Cheesecloth
 network. Members of the cheesecloth group can use the daemon's local API.
